course: dictionary
lesson: 13025
title: Facilitation: making things easier
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: «Facilitation» looks long, but it comes from a simple idea. To facilitate something is to make it easier or help it happen. Find the smaller word inside it: facilitate. The person who does the facilitating is a facilitator.
explain: Read this sentence: «Our teacher's facilitation of the debate meant that every child could speak.» The teacher did not pick a side. She guided the debate so that everyone could take part. Here, facilitation means leading a group so that it works well.
explain: «Facilitation» is a formal word. In a casual sentence you might write «help», but in a formal report «facilitation» sounds more exact. Test it by swapping: «The club's facilitation of the sports day» means the club helped the sports day happen. If your swapped word still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: The word works in science too. Sometimes one living thing helps another to grow, for example when an older tree shelters a young seedling from strong wind. Scientists call this facilitation. The same idea of helping something happen is still there.
fact: Facilitation is an uncountable noun, so we say «some facilitation» or «the facilitation of» something, not «a facilitation».
fact: It comes from «facilitate», which means to make something easier or help it happen.
fact: A facilitator leads a group discussion or meeting so that everyone can take part and work well together.
fact: In science, facilitation means one living thing helping another to grow.
fact: Useful phrases: «facilitation of» (the facilitation of learning) and «trade facilitation» (making trade between countries easier).
exercise: «Our teacher's facilitation of the group discussion helped everyone take part.» What does facilitation mean here? | Going home early | Writing the notes alone | *Guiding a group so that everyone can take part | Shouting over the others to win
exercise: Which word would a formal writer use instead of «help» in «The council's ____ of the new park was praised»? | fascination | fiction | *facilitation | fixation
exercise: In science, what does facilitation mean? | One living thing eating another | A test of how fast seeds sprout | *One living thing helping another to grow | A rock being worn away by water
test: «The facilitator asked quiet Sam to share his idea, so the whole group could join in.» What is the facilitator's job? | Ending the meeting early | *Leading the group so that everyone takes part | Choosing the best answer alone | Telling everyone to be quiet
test: Which phrase means making trade between countries easier? | trade secret | *trade facilitation | trade fair | trade wind
exam: What is the best meaning of facilitation? | *Making something easier to do or helping it happen | A grey, wet day | Making something harder to do | A loud argument in a meeting
